# Run data lives here, beside the code that produced it, and is never wiped.
#
# What is committed and what is not follows one rule: EVIDENCE is kept, BULK is
# rebuildable. Measured on 2026-09-19 the split is 12 MB of JSON against 17 GB
# of meshes and volume solutions -- and the 12 MB is what every number in the
# reports is derived from, so losing it would mean re-running to recover
# figures that were already computed.
#
# Note for anyone editing this: a `#` only starts a comment at the START of a
# line. An inline one becomes part of the pattern, which silently matches
# nothing -- that mistake is why the first version of this file admitted 29
# files instead of 923.

# Ignore everything, then allow the evidence back in.
*
!*/
!.gitignore

# per-run evidence: forces, convergence, identity, and how it got there
!result.json
!run_manifest.json
!memory_watch.json
!changes.json
!*_gate.json
!*_summary.json
!*_dataset_rows.json
!forces_breakdown.dat
!case.cfg
!history*.csv
!*.sh

# never: hundreds of MB each and reproducible from the mesher at the recorded
# commit. Their sha256 is in the evidence above, so a regenerated file can be
# checked against the one that produced a published number.
*.cgns
*.cgns.gz
*.xyz
*.vtk
*.npz
restart*.dat
run.log
run_cont*.log
*.pdf
*.png
*.tec
